WEBVTT

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:07.310
We're fighting right now in the galaxy soccer tournament, Grand Celesta Galaxy.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:11.320
Our next opponent is the planet Sazanaarah.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:15.310
We continue to fight as we aim to be best in the universe.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:23.600
I believe that this planet needs a king.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.400
A king like my father, who will lead everyone on the right path.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:32.210
That is why I want you to be king, Tsurugi.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:38.930
If you undergo the marriage ceremony with me, you can become this planet's king.

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:22.620
Why did we lose?

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.640
They weren't even that impressive.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.330
Your movements weren't bad at all.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:38.260
Just...

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:39.930
Just... what?

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.240
It was the opponent's movements that bothered me.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:46.880
They always ran ahead of the ball's trajectory, didn't they.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:47.820
Yeah.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.510
They did so all the time.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:51.810
Yeah. All of our passes got cut.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:57.260
Which means... that they were able to predict how we would move.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.530
Do you think so too, Tsurugi?

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:00.360
Sure...

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:01.730
So that's it.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:03.480
I see it!

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:07.370
The Sazanaarahns were able to stay one step ahead of us because they can predict the future.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.220
The future?

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:13.600
If they can see the future, won't they be able to see how the match will end, too?

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.770
Then there's no point playing the match to begin with.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:18.770
You're wrong on that line of thinking.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:22.740
It's not the future that the Sazanaarahns can see.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:28.310
Come to think of it, you mentioned that the people here possess a dangerous ability.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:28.680
Yes.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:33.650
Sazanaarahns are able to see the minds of others with their naked eye.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.440
See?

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.610
Not read our minds, but see them?

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.820
Yes. They can see it.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:44.400
Tell us that sooner!

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.700
I can't believe this.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:48.290
That's kind of creepy.

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:51.130
Well, I find it intriguing.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:54.920
Come to think of it, one of them talked to you, didn't they, Matatagi-kun?

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.590
That's right. What did they say to you?

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.920
O-Oh...

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.840
<i>You're a lonely guy, I see.</i>

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.640
He was just talking trash about us. Calling us weak and stuff.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:11.800
But why single you out?

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.680
I don't know.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.440
In any case, they're a dangerous opponent.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.310
Will we be able to play a proper match this way?

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:22.510
Why not? I think it's interesting.

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:26.450
It's fun thinking about how to get the upper hand over them, don't you agree?

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:27.700
Is that so?

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:32.680
Wouldn't they also be able to tell that we are thinking about how to get the upper hand?

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.580
It's possible that they will get the upper hand over our upper hand.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:41.260
There's no way we can stop ourselves from thinking about how to win during the match.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:43.860
This is a difficult problem.

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:47.760
A soccer battle?

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:51.100
Powai didn't want to hear about that.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:54.060
Who said they could do that?

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.970
It was a decision made by some of your adoring fans.

00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:01.110
While it may anger you, I ask humbly...

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:02.950
Most humbly that you show them mercy.

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:04.110
Oh, all right.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.930
But it must have shocked those Earthlings, didn't it?

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:10.640
Seeing us get to the ball before they could.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:12.640
Indeed.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:18.200
As a matter of fact, milady, there is a matter about them that you must know.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.540
What? What is it?

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:28.090
According to reports, one of the Earthlings they fought against has an extremely frightful Azul.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:32.060
This is him.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:37.060
He has a warped Azul that is dark and hideous.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:40.060
Wow! Now that's interesting!

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.520
Mind filling me in as well?

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.060
Hilary...

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:53.370
Why, if it isn't one of Falam Orbius's Shitennou, Lady Hilary Flail.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:56.020
What business do you have with us today?

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.970
It's almost time for the game.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:05:59.830
We ought to exchange information.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:03.150
The circumstances may not agree with you, but I do want us to be friends.

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:06.970
There you go again, saying stuff you're not sincerely thinking.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:10.820
What?

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:13.460
Lady Powai!

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:17.480
There's no need for you to see my mind.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:21.200
Milady, compose yourself!

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:23.970
What's your problem?

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:25.930
Felt good, didn't it?

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:29.360
My hair can drain a person's life energy.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.420
You understand now, don't you.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:36.170
Even without seeing my mind, you can see that I am amazing.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:43.330
Now, why don't we move along by telling me about this boy's frightful Azul.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:48.590
Matatagi-kun, aren't you going?

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:53.020
Everyone else is training in the Black Room.

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:55.440
There's no point training when they can see what we're thinking.

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:03.150
I wonder how your mind appears to the Sazanaarahns when you take on that attitude.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.310
I wish I could see it, too.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:09.570
I think you're more afraid of the Sazanaarahns than we are.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:12.990
You talk too much, like always.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:16.000
Bye.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.040
Matatagi!

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:19.120
I'm taking a nap.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.400
That soccer battle wore me out.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.350
What were you two talking about?

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:30.660
Since we're in a planet where our minds are laid bared, maybe it's a good idea that you know.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:34.350
It's about Matatagi-kun.

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:40.640
The Sazanaarahns probably know more about Matatagi-kun right now than we do.

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:48.530
<i>You're a lonely guy, I see.</i>

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:54.490
<i>It's no wonder you don't have any friends who care about you.</i>

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.930
Me... lonely?

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:59.370
I'm not lonely.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.150
This is normal.

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:04.500
This is how you have to act to get through everyday life.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:22.430
Hey Dad, let's build it together!

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:25.710
Hey, it's Matatagi.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:28.770
Did you come here to play Zoom Carts, too?

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:34.600
I figured out how to make the start dash go faster.

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:37.640
You just have to warm up the motor before you race it.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:38.950
It acts totally different.

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:40.290
I see.

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:44.170
Hey, there's no point telling him that.

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:46.040
Matatagi doesn't have a Zoom Cart.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:47.950
Oh, he doesn't?

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:49.040
Right?

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:52.970
I'm getting it as a present some other time.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:57.060
Oh, then I guess you wouldn't know what I was talking about earlier.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.050
Teach me next time.

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:01.240
See you, Matatagi.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.170
Yeah.

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:20.910
Hey!

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:23.000
Matatagi.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.110
Where are you going?

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:25.950
I have cram school.

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.550
I didn't know you went to cram school.

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:28.290
Yeah.

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:31.530
Hey, are you free this Saturday?

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:33.310
We're all meeting up at my house.

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:34.260
Why don't you join us?

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.750
I can't...

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:39.300
I have to look after my brothers.

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:42.240
Then you can bring your brothers, too.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:45.460
We're friends, you don't have to hold back.

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:47.910
I can't! They'll only be a bother.

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:51.900
My brothers are still small, so they might break something.

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:55.820
Well, if you say so.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:58.420
See you in school tomorrow.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:09:59.490
Yeah.

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:06.730
I'm sorry for not being able to leave the hospital quickly.

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:08.120
Don't worry about it, Mom.

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:11.020
You don't have to worry about us.

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:14.330
Yuuta is taking good care of Shun today, besides.

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:15.310
I see.

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:18.130
You're being responsible older brothers, are you.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:24.200
Mom, are you okay?

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:26.720
Yes, I'm fine.

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:29.330
Are you all eating properly?

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:30.820
Do you have enough money?

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:32.480
We've got it worked out.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:35.060
Granny, this is cool, isn't it?

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:37.360
Let me have a look.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.860
That toy is popular right now, isn't it?

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:42.070
Yeah.

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:47.830
If there's extra money left over from our budget, you can use it to buy yourself that.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.920
It's okay, buying that is a waste of money.

00:10:57.080 --> 00:11:00.460
We could never save up enough to afford it, Mom.

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:04.930
Yuuta, thanks for looking after Shun.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.600
Yay, snacks!

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.420
Only one piece per day, okay?

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:08.680
Okay!

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.140
Did you go see Mom today?

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:14.020
She looked much better.

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:15.930
When do you think she'll come back?

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:18.030
I'm not sure.

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:26.800
Hey, one of my friends said I can take you guys with me to play over at his house on Saturday.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:27.820
Do you want to go?

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:29.330
He said we can play video games together.

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:31.750
I'm going, I wanna go!

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:35.840
Then I'll tell him tomorrow that we're coming.

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:43.590
I've been wondering about Matatagi, too.

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:45.930
You, too?

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:46.930
Yeah...

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:50.130
Just before the finals...

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:55.060
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:11:56.880 --> 00:12:00.240
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:09.290
That's so cool!

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:12.600
Oh man, I wish I had that.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.930
I hope I can win it at a prize contest.

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:18.800
Can I come over to your house this Saturday after all?

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:24.640
I talked with my brothers and they said they wanted to come.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:25.180
It's okay, right?

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:27.890
Sorry, Saturday is a bad day.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:30.770
I see...

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:34.280
We started talking about playing Zoom Carts in cram school.

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:39.260
You don't have a Zoom Cart, so even if you came, you'd be bored.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:43.150
Matatagi said he was coming.

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:44.650
Seriously?

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:46.200
What can he do when he's there?

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:50.240
I turned him down, but he took it seriously.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.440
He's such a downer.

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:52.160
Yeah.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:05.090
If you have a lottery ticket, step right up and try your luck!

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:11.890
We have a winner!

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:14.600
You won third place, kid!

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:19.110
We have a lot of prizes for third place. Pick whichever one you want!

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:21.150
That one!

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:23.330
I want the Zoom Cart!

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:47.550
You told me.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.550
You told me we were friends.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:53.640
It's not me they want to be with.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.060
It's this thing that they want.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:00.770
Friends?

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:03.400
That's a downright lie.

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:05.780
This is how people really are.

00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:08.770
People can't be trusted.

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:10.820
I can't depend on any of them.

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:17.510
What a stupid thing to remember.

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:20.310
Hello?

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:22.130
It's me, Shinsuke!

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:23.800
Want to come practice with us?

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:26.060
Hey!

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:28.260
Come with us.

00:14:28.710 --> 00:14:33.420
We started talking about what formations we could test out that will be the most effective.

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:35.390
So we need you.

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:37.040
Sounds like a plan.

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:38.850
Okay, I'll come.

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:44.570
<i>You're a lonely guy, I see.</i>

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:50.320
<i>It's no wonder you don't have any friends who care about you.</i>

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.020
Me, lonely?

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.110
I'm pulling it off well.

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:59.130
I'm responding maturely and getting along with everyone.

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:10.040
That's good!

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:11.860
Matatagi, to Tsurugi!

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:12.590
And then shoot!

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:20.220
Sorry, one more time.

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:22.440
What's wrong? Your plays have been acting up.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:24.420
Really?

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:27.900
The way you handle the ball seems different from usual.

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:31.640
Is that how I look?

00:15:32.020 --> 00:15:34.170
Um, yeah...

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:35.870
It's just your imagination.

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:38.680
Is something about Tsurugi-kun bothering you?

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.770
I don't know?

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:47.680
There's something strange about him.

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:48.380
Strange as in what?

00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:51.840
I can't explain it very well, but...

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:55.310
Tsurugi-kun doesn't use his towel like that.

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:56.840
I'm surprised you know that.

00:15:56.840 --> 00:15:57.810
I know everyone's habits.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:02.600
When you're in front of a mirror, you stand there looking at your face for 15 minutes.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.810
Personal grooming! It's personal grooming!

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:07.820
Something's not right...

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:10.570
He doesn't feel like Tsurugi-kun.

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:19.330
Something wrong?

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:21.880
Oh, nothing.

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:26.170
Captain was worried about you earlier, so we just wondered if you were okay.

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:26.880
Right?

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:27.950
Right.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:31.920
I'm distracted thinking about how to fight the Sazanaarahns.

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:33.730
That's why I'm not at my best.

00:16:33.730 --> 00:16:35.950
Yeah, I thought so!

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:37.400
It's the same for me, too.

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:39.060
I mean, who wants their thoughts to be seen by other people?

00:16:39.820 --> 00:16:42.130
Oh, I know! We could surprise them!

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:47.110
Like, how about Tsurugi-kun keeps missing all of the shoots even though you're a striker?

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:50.130
Then while they're confused, the rest of us can make the shoot.

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:51.130
Like me.

00:16:51.130 --> 00:16:52.000
Or Konoha.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:52.600
Eh?

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:53.950
Heh.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:55.160
I'll talk about it with Tenma.

00:16:56.930 --> 00:16:59.880
That was more like the usual Tsurugi-kun.

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:01.020
See?

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.660
That way he goes "heh" is how he always laughs.

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:12.030
That was close.

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:12.920
I let my guard down.

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:18.550
Matsukaze Tenma knows Tsurugi Kyousuke best of all.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:20.750
He is the one you must avoid all suspicion from.

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:22.430
It's been taken care of.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:29.220
I've already copied Tsurugi Kyousuke's memory library from his brainwaves to mine,

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:32.440
and I am reproducing Tsurugi's personality to perfection.

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:33.610
Good.

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:39.120
From that information, you can duplicate his soccer plays as well.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:41.310
Understood.

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:50.840
None of us are able to find a solution yet as to how we can fight against a team that can see our minds.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:53.550
I was wondering if you had any suggestions...

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:54.820
Shindou.

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:56.340
I have one question.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:56.550
Sir?

00:17:57.370 --> 00:18:02.560
Are you all so incompetent that you cannot win without my advice?

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:15.640
What did you want to talk about?

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:22.620
The truth is, I talked once with your brothers before we played the Asia district preliminary finals.

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:27.330
They really surprised me when they told me...

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:31.330
<i>Nii-chan said winning the championship is probably impossible.</i>

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.750
That's a lie, right?

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:38.340
There's a bit of a misunderstanding involved.

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:46.240
I said that winning the championship would probably be impossible unless the team came together to fight.

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:48.100
Oh, I see.

00:18:48.930 --> 00:18:51.040
Sorry if it sounded misleading.

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:53.480
No, I don't mind.

00:18:55.910 --> 00:19:01.780
Minaho said he'd be interested in having the power to see other people's minds, but I wouldn't.

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:07.790
I think that humans are human because they have both good and bad in them.

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:14.310
Playing soccer means scuffling for the ball with everything you have while guessing the opponent's next move.

00:19:14.310 --> 00:19:17.300
When the ball is taken from you, you feel frustrated about losing it...

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:21.950
But I think that's what makes soccer fun.

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:26.480
So, it would be boring to know what a person is thinking from the beginning.

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:29.310
It certainly is boring.

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:36.330
Tomorrow, whether they see my mind or not, I'm going to play with everything I've got.

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:37.780
I'm just going to play my soccer.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:42.170
So... you should too, Matatagi.

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:42.740
Okay.

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.550
Is that what you wanted to talk to me about?

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:48.370
Yeah, I guess.

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:50.750
I just wanted to say that we can count on each other tomorrow.

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:53.250
Yeah, let's do our best.

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:03.370
Pixie.

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:05.800
Do you think I was able to get my feelings across to him?

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:12.520
Yeah. I'll take it slow.

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:17.000
So what if they can see my mind!

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.930
I'll just push right through them!

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:23.570
Hey.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:24.450
Are you okay?

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:27.510
They wouldn't need to see your mind to figure you out.

00:20:27.510 --> 00:20:30.200
No, wait, maybe that's a good plan.

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:33.820
We should be more assertive and use our voices.

00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:35.060
I know!

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:38.480
What about calling out "Captain!" but sending the pass to Tsurugi-kun instead?

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:39.300
Wait!

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:43.640
When you make the pass, your mind will turn its focus onto Tsurugi-san.

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:45.300
Once they see that, it's over.

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:47.570
I see...

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:50.810
Then what do we do?!

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:54.600
We're facing a particularly tough opponent this time.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:56.110
Here I go, Ibuki!

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:03.990
Why can't I block them?!

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:06.600
Don't leave it all to chance.

00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:09.990
You need to get into the same mindset as your opponent in order to predict how they will come at you.

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:13.370
The same mindset...

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:18.330
Did you hear what Shindou-kun just said?

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:22.660
Leave it all to chance... Get into the same mindset as the opponent...

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:26.000
This may turn out to be the big hint that helps us win.

00:22:53.880 --> 00:22:56.680
Our match on the water planet Sazanaarah begins.

00:22:56.680 --> 00:23:01.230
Is there a way we can win, when they can see what we're thinking?

00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:04.400
Next, Awaken! My Dark Side!!

00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:06.530
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:19.640
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:26.640
Humans are human because they have both good and bad in them!

00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:27.730
That's all!
